ant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Tennessee remains one of the most Republican-leaning states in presidential politics, with a partisan lean of roughly 14 points toward the GOP. With the incumbent term-limited, the race is open, but no general-election polls, expert ratings, or market pricing exist specifically for the presidential contest, so the forecast rests on fundamentals. A September poll showed Trump's approval underwater in the state, and Democratic governors with national ambitions are putting money into Tennessee races, suggesting some added Democratic energy.\n\nThose tailwinds are modest against a durable Republican advantage. The forecast expects the Republican to carry the state comfortably, with enough residual uncertainty from thin data to keep it short of Safe R.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0603, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1012, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.11, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1055, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0961, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1038, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0969, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1086, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.082, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0965, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.1008, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0993, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0988, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.1057, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0921, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.0979, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.104, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.0893, "margin": -14.0}]}